id distribution.\n   - All these remaining (half-filled barrels) must equate to fulfill \\(k\\) half-filled barrels overall. This ensures feasible non-negative assignments.\n\n6. **Empty Barrels:**\n   - Each truck effectively gets \\(A, B,\\) and \\(C\\) empty barrels correspondingly.\n   \n7. **Number of Possible Configurations:**\n   - The problem boils down to counting the number of solutions to equation (1) that fulfill conditions (2) under the constraint \\(k = 7\\).\n   - Derive valid sequences (\\(A, B, C\\)) considering non-differentiable orders:\n     - Each truck assignment: [ \\{ \\(A, B, C\\) \\}, without regard to ordering].\n\n8. **Case Analysis:**\n   - **Case 1:** \\(3 + 3 + 1\\)\n   - **Case 2:** \\(3 + 2 + 2\\)\n   \nSo, the number of solutions (each configuration valid per given condition):\n\nConclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "In the quadrilateral $ABCD$, all four sides are tangent to a circle with center $O$. Express the sum of the angles $AOB$ and $COD$ in terms of the angles of the quadrilateral, as well as the sum of the angles $BOC$ and $DOA$, for the following scenarios:\n\nI. All four points of tangency lie on the sides of the quadrilateral.\n\nII. Two sides are tangent to the circle at points outside the sides of the quadrilateral.\n\nIII. All four sides are tangent to the circle at points outside the sides of the quadrilateral.", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, so I have this problem about quadrilaterals tangent to a circle, which makes me think of tangential quadrilaterals. The question is in three parts, I, II, and III, each dealing with different scenarios of where the points of tangency lie. The goal is to express the sum of angles AOB and COD, and the sum of angles BOC and DOA in terms of the angles of the quadrilateral. Let me start by recalling some properties of tangential quadrilaterals.\n\nFirst, in a tangential quadrilateral, the 