 \\cdot z_2 = \\left( \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot x + \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot yi - \\frac{1}{2}i \\cdot x - \\frac{1}{2}i \\cdot yi \\right)\n    \\]\n\n6. Combine like terms:\n    \\[\n    \\overline{z_1} \\cdot z_2 = \\left( \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} x - \\frac{1}{2} y \\right) + \\left( \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} y - \\frac{1}{2} x \\right)i\n    \\]\n\n7. The real part must be zero (given condition):\n    \\[\n    \\operatorname{Re} \\left[ \\overline{z_1} \\cdot z_2 \\right] = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} x - \\frac{1}{2} y = 0\n    \\]\n    Solve for \\( x \\):\n    \\[\n    \\sqrt{3} x = y \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{3}}\n    \\]\n\n8. Since \\( z_2 \\) also lies on the circle, we have:\n    \\[\n    x^2 + (y-1)^2 = 1\n    \\]\n\n9. Substitute \\( x = \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{3}} \\) into the circle equation:\n    \\[\n    \\left( \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{3}} \\right)^2 + (y-1)^2 = 1\n    \\]\n    Simplify:\n    \\[\n    \\frac{y^2}{3} + y^2 - 2y + 1 = 1\n    \\]\n    Combine the terms:\n    \\[\n    \\frac{4y^2}{3} - 2y = 0\n    \\]\n\n10. Solve for \\( y \\):\n    \\[\n    4y^2 - 6y = 0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad y(4y - 6) = 0\n    \\]\n    The solutions are:\n    \\[\n    y = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad y = \\frac{3}{2}\n    \\]\n\n11. \\( y= 0 \\) leads to \\( z_2 = 0 \\), which we discard since \\( z_2 \\neq 0 \\).\n\n12. Therefore, \\( y = \\frac{3}{2} \\).\n\n13. Substitute \\( y = \\frac{3}{2} \\) back into \\( x = \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{3}} \\):\n    \\[\n    x = \\frac{\\frac{3}{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n    \\]\n\n14. Conclude \\( z_2 \\):\n    \\[\n    z_2 = x + yi = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{3}{2}i\n    \\]\n\nFinally, \\( z_2 = -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{3}{2}i \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{3}{2}i}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Find the probability of a simultaneous occurrence of a specific digit when tossing two coins once